<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">=F0=9F=94=AC What Make=
s a Principal-Level Answer</h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Example: "How would you =
implement useState?"</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Junior Answer</strong>: =
"I would use useRef to store the value and return it with a setter function=
."</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Senior Answer</strong>: =
"useState needs to integrate with React's fiber reconciliation. It requires=
 a hook data structure linked to the component instance, a dispatch mechani=
sm that schedules updates, and proper state comparison to prevent unnecessa=
ry re-renders."</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Principal Answer</strong=
>: "useState is part of React's broader state management strategy. Implemen=
tation involves fiber hooks linked list, update queues with priority schedu=
ling, bailout mechanisms for performance, integration with Concurrent Mode,=
 v=C3=A0 considerations for server-side rendering. At scale, we also need t=
o consider memory usage patterns, state batching strategies, v=C3=A0 develo=
per experience through DevTools integration."</p>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">=F0=9F=92=A1 Interview=
 Red Flags vs Green Flags</h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=F0=9F=9A=A9 Red Flags:<=
/strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Can't explain "why" behind impl=
ementations</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Doesn't consider error cases</l=
i>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">No mention of performance impli=
cations</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Treats interview as algorithm c=
ontest instead of engineering discussion</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Can't connect concepts to real-=
world usage</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=E2=9C=85 Green Flags:</=
strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Asks clarifying questions about=
 requirements</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Discusses trade-offs v=C3=A0 al=
ternatives</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Mentions testing strategies</li=
>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Considers user experience impli=
cations</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Shows understanding of producti=
on constraints</li>
</ul>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">=F0=9F=8E=AF How to In=
terview Like a Principal</h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Framework for Evaluating=
 Candidates:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Technical Foundation</s=
trong>: Do they understand core concepts deeply?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>System Thinking</strong=
>: Can they see how parts connect to whole?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Problem Solving</strong=
>: Do they break down complex problems systematically?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Communication</strong>:=
 Can they explain technical concepts clearly?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Growth Mindset</strong>=
: Do they learn from mistakes v=C3=A0 ask good questions?</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Sample Follow-up Questio=
ns:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Instead of: "Implement useStat=
e"
Ask: "How would you design a state management system for a large React appl=
ication? What are the trade-offs between different approaches?"</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Instead of: "Sort these versio=
ns"
Ask: "You're building a package manager. How would you handle version resol=
ution with thousands of packages v=C3=A0 complex dependency graphs?"</p>
<hr>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">K=E1=BA=BET LU=
=E1=BA=ACN: T=E1=BB=AA INTERVIEW =C4=90=E1=BA=BEN MASTERY</h2>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">=F0=9F=8C=9F Key=
 Insights for Engineering Growth</h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Qua analysis c=E1=BB=A7a intervi=
ew experience n=C3=A0y, nh=E1=BB=AFng lessons quan tr=E1=BB=8Dng nh=E1=BA=
=A5t:</p>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">1. <strong>Depth Over =
Breadth in Understanding</strong></h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">=F0=9F=92=AD <strong>Principal's=
 Reflection</strong>: Sau 15+ years, t=C3=B4i realized r=E1=BA=B1ng junior =
engineers often try to learn "all the frameworks", nh=C6=B0ng senior engine=
ers focus on understanding fundamental principles deeply. A senior who trul=
y understands closure v=C3=A0 event loops s=E1=BA=BD excel v=E1=BB=9Bi b=E1=
=BA=A5t k=E1=BB=B3 JavaScript framework n=C3=A0o.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Action Items:</strong></=
p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Pick one concept weekly v=C3=A0=
 study it t=E1=BB=AB first principles</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Implement core features yoursel=
f (e.g., build your own state management)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Read source code c=E1=BB=A7a li=
braries you use daily</li>
</ul>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">2. <strong>System Thin=
king Beats Algorithmic Skills</strong></h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Interview algorithms quan tr=E1=
=BB=8Dng, nh=C6=B0ng production engineering c=E1=BA=A7n system thinking. Ab=
ility to see connections, anticipate failures, v=C3=A0 design for scale mat=
ter more than optimizing bubble sort.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Development Path:</stron=
g></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Study large-scale system archit=
ectures (Netflix, Google, Facebook)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Practice designing systems cho =
real-world constraints</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Learn from production incidents=
 v=C3=A0 postmortems</li>
</ul>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">3. <strong>Communicati=
on is Technical Skill</strong></h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Candidate trong interview c=C3=
=B3 solid technical knowledge nh=C6=B0ng struggled to explain concepts clea=
rly. At senior+ levels, your impact scales through others.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Practice Strategies:</st=
rong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Write technical blog posts</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Mentor junior developers</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Present at team meetings</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Practice explaining complex con=
cepts simply</li>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">=F0=9F=9A=80 Nex=
t Steps for Different Career Levels</h3>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1"><strong>For Junior Eng=
